imgsensor: ov02b10: stand by before rewriting mode registers

The mode tables reprogram PLL and timing (page 1 0x0e/0x0f, 0x14/0x15), and
the setters are reached mid-stream on a preview->capture switch. Putting the
sensor in standby around that is the sequence the hardware expects; the
reference driver got it for free from the newer imgsensor framework issuing
SENSOR_FEATURE_SET_STREAMING_SUSPEND/RESUME, which this platform's HAL never
sends.

Tried as a fix for takePicture timing out on ISP_WAIT_IRQ and it did NOT fix
that - see docs/findings.md. Kept only because the sequence is correct.

--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/mt8163/ov02b10_mipi_raw/ov02b10mipiraw_Sensor.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/mt8163/ov02b10_mipi_raw/ov02b10mipiraw_Sensor.c
@@ -591,6 +591,22 @@
 
 static void preview_setting(void)
 {
+	/* Put the sensor in standby before rewriting the mode registers.
+	 *
+	 * These tables reprogram PLL and timing (page 1 0x0e/0x0f, 0x14/0x15),
+	 * and the mode setters are reached mid-stream on a preview->capture
+	 * switch, so this is the sequence the hardware expects. The reference
+	 * driver got it from the newer imgsensor framework issuing
+	 * SENSOR_FEATURE_SET_STREAMING_SUSPEND/RESUME around a mode change,
+	 * which this platform's HAL never sends, so bracket it here instead.
+	 *
+	 * NOTE: this was tried as a fix for takePicture timing out on
+	 * ISP_WAIT_IRQ (pass 1 TG1_DON, status 0x400) and it did NOT fix it -
+	 * the capture still times out identically. Kept because standby before
+	 * reprogramming is correct regardless, but do not mistake it for a fix.
+	 */
+	streaming_control(KAL_FALSE);
+
 
 	write_cmos_sensor(0xfc, 0x01);
 	write_cmos_sensor(0xfd, 0x00);
@@ -696,6 +712,22 @@
 
